@startuml
title Prepwise — Secure mock-test lifecycle
actor Student
boundary Browser
control "Flask test route" as Route
control "Flask-Login / owner check" as Auth
control "Test scoring logic" as Scorer
database SQLite
Student -> Browser: Select published test
Browser -> Route: POST /mock-tests/{id}/start
Route -> Auth: Require authenticated student
Auth --> Route: Active user identity
Route -> SQLite: Create in_progress TestAttempt
SQLite --> Route: attempt id + server started_at
Route --> Browser: Redirect to attempt
Browser -> Route: GET /test-attempts/{attempt}
Route -> Auth: Verify owner or admin
Route -> SQLite: Load test questions/options
note right of Route
  Correct answer keys are not
  serialized to the browser.
end note
SQLite --> Route: Question text and choices
Route --> Browser: Render test and remaining time
Student -> Browser: Select options and submit
Browser -> Route: POST answer IDs and choices
Route -> Auth: Re-check attempt ownership/state
Route -> SQLite: Load allowed test question IDs and keys
SQLite --> Route: Authoritative test configuration
Route -> Scorer: Validate choices and calculate marks
Scorer --> Route: Score, percentage, answer review
Route -> SQLite: Persist answers and submitted attempt
Route -> Scorer: Refresh rule-based suggestions
Scorer -> SQLite: Store recommendations
Route --> Browser: Redirect to result
Browser -> Route: GET private result
Route -> Auth: Verify result owner or admin
Route -> SQLite: Load score and answer review
SQLite --> Route: Persisted result records
Route --> Browser: Render result and explanations
@enduml
